RAHS — Region-Aware Hierarchical Sub-Feature Alignment

This release reorganizes and modifies aWeirdName/iclr26_exp1 at commit
b9c8eb4cffe0d95440496b1c55ed3efba345b71a.
https://github.com/aWeirdName/iclr26_exp1

The experimental repository is derived from Uncertainty-aware Blur Prior (UBP):
Haitao Wu, Qing Li, Changqing Zhang, Zhen He, Xiaomin Ying.
Bridging the Vision-Brain Gap with an Uncertainty-Aware Blur Prior, CVPR 2025.
https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.04207
The Apache License 2.0 supplied with that repository is retained in LICENSE.

rahs/model.py and rahs/losses.py adapt the active EEG encoder and alignment
objectives. rahs/data.py and rahs/preprocess.py adapt the original data contract
and preprocessing protocol. These files have been reorganized and modified;
see docs/reproducibility.md for behavioral differences.

rahs/resampler.py derives from the experimental emb_gen/resamper.py, which uses
IP-Adapter's resampler and credits the following sources:
https://github.com/tencent-ailab/IP-Adapter
https://github.com/mlfoundations/open_flamingo/blob/main/open_flamingo/src/helpers.py
https://github.com/lucidrains/imagen-pytorch/blob/main/imagen_pytorch/imagen_pytorch.py
The retained adaptation exposes intermediate latents and attention weights.
Pretrained IP-Adapter/CLIP weights and all datasets are distributed separately.
